Viśvāmitra asks r̥ṣis to sacrifice for bodily Triśaṅku ascent --- R̥ṣis agree fearing his curse --- Viśvāmitra officiates while priests perform rites --- Gods refuse their invoked shares --- Viśvāmitra hurls Triśaṅku bodily heavenward by tapas power --- Indra casts Triśaṅku headlong back toward earth --- Viśvāmitra halts his fall, creates southern Saptar̥ṣis and stars, threatens new Indra and gods --- Gods grant Triśaṅku headlong refuge outside Vaiśvānara path; all depart